1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,783
For eight lectures, you've drawn every floor your crew walked on.

2
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:08,757
Today they board a ship,

3
00:00:09,207 --> 00:00:10,946
and you draw nothing.

4
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:15,759
The game builds her deck from her own plan.

5
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,167
Your job is what's on it.

6
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:24,546
A prisoner, a gunner who won't give up,

7
00:00:24,996 --> 00:00:28,474
and a strongbox that ends it three ways.

8
00:00:30,274 --> 00:00:38,100
It's brand new, so at the end I'll show you what to check before your crew finds it.

9
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,474
The button needs four things.

10
00:00:42,374 --> 00:00:44,548
A ship that has struck.

11
00:00:44,998 --> 00:00:47,172
A hull with a plan.

12
00:00:47,622 --> 00:00:51,100
The station art, which your starter already has.

13
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,074
And no other party out.

14
00:00:55,974 --> 00:00:58,583
That last one is the trouble.

15
00:01:00,383 --> 00:01:03,861
Your relay party opens in the first second,

16
00:01:04,311 --> 00:01:08,659
and a party on a map never closes by itself.

17
00:01:09,559 --> 00:01:11,733
So as your mission stands,

18
00:01:12,183 --> 00:01:15,226
with anybody still down at the relay,

19
00:01:15,676 --> 00:01:18,720
Comms can't send a party to her.

20
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:23,128
We fix that with one rule.

21
00:01:23,578 --> 00:01:27,057
When she strikes, the landing party comes home.

22
00:01:27,957 --> 00:01:31,870
When the ship comes back, the relay opens again.

23
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:36,113
Here she is on the Comms console,

24
00:01:36,563 --> 00:01:40,476
the Black Gull, a pirate, out past the relay.

25
00:01:41,376 --> 00:01:44,420
Hail, taunt, or tell her to surrender.

26
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:51,002
In the file, first a side for her to be on.

27
00:01:51,452 --> 00:01:54,930
One record, and one line that says enemies.

28
00:01:56,730 --> 00:01:59,774
Then the ship, in the story file.

29
00:02:00,224 --> 00:02:03,267
Two lines, under the relay's own line.

30
00:02:05,067 --> 00:02:09,415
Her hull is a pirate raider, with no fighter bay.

31
00:02:10,315 --> 00:02:12,489
A carrier brings its fighters,

32
00:02:12,939 --> 00:02:16,417
and they'd shoot at your ship all game.

33
00:02:18,217 --> 00:02:19,957
Look at the numbers.

34
00:02:20,857 --> 00:02:24,335
The first set is where she comes from.

35
00:02:24,785 --> 00:02:27,393
The second is where she is.

36
00:02:29,193 --> 00:02:34,846
That matters, because a ship that strikes and isn't boarded runs for home,

37
00:02:35,296 --> 00:02:39,643
and when she gets there she's taken off the map.

38
00:02:40,543 --> 00:02:43,152
I tried it with one place.

39
00:02:43,602 --> 00:02:47,515
She struck, and eight seconds later she was gone.

40
00:02:48,715 --> 00:02:52,193
Here's the chase in the Quest Log aboard,

41
00:02:52,643 --> 00:02:55,252
with her picture at the top.

42
00:02:57,052 --> 00:03:00,096
In the file there are three quests.

43
00:03:00,996 --> 00:03:06,213
Run her down, which waits for the ship to close on her.

44
00:03:07,113 --> 00:03:11,461
Come back to the relay, which is hidden until then.

45
00:03:12,361 --> 00:03:17,143
And take her, which waits for a signal the game sends.

46
00:03:18,943 --> 00:03:22,857
Two of them get a page for the bridge.

47
00:03:23,307 --> 00:03:26,785
Her picture at the top of the chase,

48
00:03:27,235 --> 00:03:30,278
and two icon bullets on the prize.

49
00:03:32,078 --> 00:03:34,687
The card is one you know.

50
00:03:35,137 --> 00:03:38,615
It's the tug card from the first class,

51
00:03:39,065 --> 00:03:41,239
hearing a different step start.

52
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:44,778
It does two things.

53
00:03:45,228 --> 00:03:49,141
It calls the landing party home, and she strikes.

54
00:03:50,941 --> 00:03:54,854
And the same line goes on your old card,

55
00:03:55,304 --> 00:03:57,043
for the trip back.

56
00:03:58,243 --> 00:04:02,591
Here's her deck, and the captain's strongbox, in her brig.

57
00:04:04,391 --> 00:04:08,304
In the file, two new words put it there.

58
00:04:09,204 --> 00:04:12,683
Area, deck: that means whatever ship we board.

59
00:04:14,483 --> 00:04:18,830
And mark is no longer a mark in a file,

60
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:21,454
because there is no file.

61
00:04:22,354 --> 00:04:24,528
It's a kind of room.

62
00:04:24,978 --> 00:04:26,717
Brig, cargo, quarters, bay.

63
00:04:28,517 --> 00:04:31,561
Her hold is called the plunder hold.

64
00:04:32,011 --> 00:04:34,185
Her sickbay is the surgery.

65
00:04:35,085 --> 00:04:37,693
You don't need to know that.

66
00:04:38,143 --> 00:04:42,491
You write the kind, and it works on any hull.

67
00:04:44,291 --> 00:04:47,770
And when a hull has no such room,

68
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:53,437
your thing stands in the hallway, and the game says so once.

69
00:04:54,637 --> 00:04:56,376
Here's her deck again.

70
00:04:57,276 --> 00:04:59,450
Nobody stands about on it

71
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,074
but the people you wrote.

72
00:05:03,874 --> 00:05:07,787
A calm person blocks the cell they stand on,

73
00:05:08,237 --> 00:05:10,411
and so does a strongbox.

74
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:16,093
So the game walks the deck before it puts anything down.

75
00:05:16,993 --> 00:05:20,037
Nothing of yours stands in a doorway,

76
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:23,530
or anywhere that would shut something in.

77
00:05:25,330 --> 00:05:30,113
Where a thing stands can change when you add a record.

78
00:05:30,563 --> 00:05:34,476
What it can never do is block the way.

79
00:05:36,276 --> 00:05:40,624
So keep one rule: after every change to what's aboard,

80
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:44,117
go aboard and walk to each thing.

81
00:05:45,317 --> 00:05:47,057
Now play it through.

82
00:05:47,957 --> 00:05:51,435
Helm closes to fifteen hundred, and she strikes.

83
00:05:52,335 --> 00:05:55,378
Comms selects her, and sends a party.

84
00:05:57,178 --> 00:06:00,657
Aboard, the gunner waits in the boat bay.

85
00:06:01,557 --> 00:06:04,165
She sees anyone within four cells,

86
00:06:04,615 --> 00:06:07,659
and one hit can put them down.

87
00:06:09,459 --> 00:06:12,067
So one of you goes aft,

88
00:06:12,517 --> 00:06:14,691
a cell at a time.

89
00:06:15,591 --> 00:06:19,070
The moment she's in sight, five cells off,

90
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:22,128
fire, full, arm, and click her.

91
00:06:23,028 --> 00:06:24,767
Shots miss a lot,

92
00:06:25,217 --> 00:06:29,565
and no app tells you a shot hit or missed.

93
00:06:31,365 --> 00:06:33,104
If she downs somebody,

94
00:06:33,554 --> 00:06:36,598
the boarding kit gets them up again.

95
00:06:37,048 --> 00:06:38,352
Pack, use medkit.

96
00:06:40,152 --> 00:06:43,196
The strongbox has three answers that matter.

97
00:06:44,096 --> 00:06:47,139
Take her, and she joins your side,

98
00:06:47,589 --> 00:06:49,328
and the quest pays.

99
00:06:50,228 --> 00:06:52,402
Scuttle her, and she's gone.

100
00:06:53,302 --> 00:06:56,346
Leave her, and she runs for home.

101
00:06:58,146 --> 00:07:02,059
Every one of them brings the party home first.

102
00:07:02,959 --> 00:07:04,698
And after every one,

103
00:07:05,148 --> 00:07:09,061
the relay opens again when the ship comes back.

104
00:07:10,261 --> 00:07:13,304
Lint says clean on your finished mission.

105
00:07:14,204 --> 00:07:17,683
What's left to know isn't in your file.

106
00:07:19,483 --> 00:07:22,091
A shot never removes a prop.

107
00:07:22,991 --> 00:07:26,470
The strongbox is safe from a full shot,

108
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:30,833
and so is anything else that holds an ending.

109
00:07:32,633 --> 00:07:36,111
Comms has its own button, take as prize.

110
00:07:36,561 --> 00:07:40,039
It finishes the same quest as your strongbox,

111
00:07:40,489 --> 00:07:44,402
but nobody goes aboard to meet what you wrote.

112
00:07:46,202 --> 00:07:50,985
What the gunner drops is lost if nobody picks it up.

113
00:07:52,785 --> 00:07:57,133
And from her deck, the transporter still reaches your relay.

114
00:07:58,033 --> 00:08:01,076
Know these before your crew finds them.

115
00:08:02,276 --> 00:08:04,015
Now it's your turn.

116
00:08:04,915 --> 00:08:06,654
Play all three endings.

117
00:08:07,554 --> 00:08:11,902
Move the strongbox into the cabin, and walk to it.

118
00:08:12,802 --> 00:08:17,585
Swap her hull for a freighter, and see where everything goes.

119
00:08:19,385 --> 00:08:22,863
Then light the beacon with the gunner's cell.

120
00:08:23,763 --> 00:08:26,807
Next time, the mission is your own.
